/**
 * Frozen transcript of the pre-plugin CodenamesGameRoom.
 *
 * Captured before the M3.6 migration with a zeroed CSPRNG, so the starting team,
 * the 25-card key, the word order and the lobby shuffle are reproducible:
 *
 * - 17 steps across five rooms: the lobby (auto-filled seats, explicit roles,
 *   reset, randomize), a full clue/guess cycle with a correct guess, a neutral
 *   card, a wrong-team card, an explicit stop and a turn timeout, then a match
 *   won by contacting every agent, a match lost on the assassin, the overall
 *   clock ending an unfinished board, and a lobby that cannot start;
 * - 10 refusals with status code, English message and error code;
 * - 75 audit events in order;
 * - the replay document from the assassin match.
 *
 * Every step records all four seats and a watcher, because the whole game is a
 * privacy rule: only the two spymasters may read the key. Platform-owned clocks,
 * ids and activity timestamps are excluded.
 */

